1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,928
Yama walked away
with Satyavan's life…

2
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:07,675
And Savitri? She stood up…
and followed Death.

3
00:00:07,725 --> 00:00:10,395
Savitri and Satyavan's story…

4
00:00:10,395 --> 00:00:14,865
“A clever trick,” they say…
the Mahabharata says otherwise.

5
00:00:14,915 --> 00:00:17,425
Yama said: “Go back.”

6
00:00:17,425 --> 00:00:20,777
She said: “Where my
husband goes, I go.”

7
00:00:20,827 --> 00:00:24,265
She kept walking beside him,
speaking of goodness.

8
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:28,300
Yama: “Ask a boon…
anything but his life.”

9
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:31,793
Four boons… four times,
the same condition.

10
00:00:31,843 --> 00:00:34,607
Savitri, in the
Vana Parva:

11
00:00:34,657 --> 00:00:42,831
“Seven steps together
make a friend.”

12
00:00:44,091 --> 00:00:47,411
Saptapadam… seven steps.

13
00:00:47,411 --> 00:00:50,452
Walk seven steps together…
and you're friends.

14
00:00:50,502 --> 00:00:53,804
Savitri didn't fight Death…
she befriended him.

15
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:57,235
The fifth time… Yama dropped
the condition himself.

16
00:00:57,285 --> 00:01:02,390
“Your words keep raising my
respect… ask for anything.”

17
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:05,207
Savitri said:
“Let Satyavan live.”

18
00:01:05,257 --> 00:01:07,157
Someone said “no”?

19
00:01:07,157 --> 00:01:11,651
Don't fight. Walk with them,
listen… then ask again, kindly.

20
00:01:11,701 --> 00:01:14,726
Whose “no” should
become a “yes”?

21
00:01:14,776 --> 00:01:18,358
Savitri didn't defeat Death…
she made him a friend.
